        self.body.append(self.body[-1])
```

However, a more correct implementation would be to add the new segment in the opposite direction of the last segment:

```python
class Snake:
    def grow(self):
        last_segment = self.body[-1]
        second_last_segment = self.body[-2]
        new_segment = (last_segment[0] - (last_segment[0] - second_last_segment[0]), 
                       last_segment[1] - (last_segment[1] - second_last_segment[1]))
        self.body.append(new_segment)
